  <worksheets>
    <worksheet name='Cost of Production by Category'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#b6992d'>&lt;Sheet Name&gt;: Jonathan Williams</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Chart Type: Horizontal Bar Chart
Dual Axis: N
Reference Line: N
Trend Line: N
Calculated Fields: 1 (Total Cost by Category)
Table Calculations: 0
LOD Calculations: 0
Mark Cards: 0
Filters: 2
Visualization: To prevent overwhelming the audience, I limited the categories to 10 and utilized a horizontal bar graph to depict the annual costs of products within certain categories. By multiplying the unit cost by the number of items purchased in each category, I could determine which product categories are the most costly overall. The filter option enables users to view the most expensive category for each specific year or across all years.

Analysis: It appears that technology products are not only the most profitable but also the most expensive to manufacture, as indicated by the data.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Categories Sheet+ (Regional_Sales) (2)' name='federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6'>
            <column caption='Total Cost ' datatype='real' name='[Calculation_975029375894609921]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='SUM([UnitCost]*[OrderQuantity])' />
            </column>
            <column datatype='string' name='[Category]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column caption='Order Date' datatype='date' name='[OrderDate]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
            <column caption='Order Quantity' datatype='integer' name='[OrderQuantity]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column caption='Unit Cost' datatype='real' name='[UnitCost]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Category]' derivation='None' name='[none:Category:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Calculation_975029375894609921]' derivation='User' name='[usr:Calculation_975029375894609921:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[OrderDate]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:OrderDate:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[none:Category:nk]'>
            <groupfilter count='10' end='top' function='end' units='records' user:ui-marker='end' user:ui-top-by-field='true'>
              <groupfilter direction='DESC' expression='[Calculation_975029375894609921]' function='order' user:ui-marker='order'>
                <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[none:Category:nk]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
              </groupfilter>
            </groupfilter>
          </filter>
          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[yr:OrderDate:ok]'>
            <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[yr:OrderDate:ok]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
          </filter>
          <shelf-sorts>
            <shelf-sort-v2 dimension-to-sort='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[none:Category:nk]' direction='DESC' is-on-innermost-dimension='true' measure-to-sort-by='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[usr:Calculation_975029375894609921:qk]' shelf='rows' />
          </shelf-sorts>
          <slices>
            <column>[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[none:Category:nk]</column>
            <column>[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[yr:OrderDate:ok]</column>
          </slices>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='label'>
            <format attr='text-format' field='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[usr:Calculation_975029375894609921:qk]' value='c&quot;$&quot;#,##0;(&quot;$&quot;#,##0)' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='quick-filter'>
            <format attr='title' field='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[yr:OrderDate:ok]' value='Year'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run>Year</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </format>
          </style-rule>
        </style>
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
