    <worksheet name='Cost/Profit Text Table'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#59a14f'>&lt;Sheet Name&gt;: Jonathan Williams</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Chart Type: Text Table
Dual Axis: N
Reference Line: N
Trend Line: N
Calculated Fields: 3 (Total Cost, Unit Profit, Number of Orders)
Table Calculations: 2
LOD Calculations: 0
Mark Cards: 1
Filters: 4 
Visualization: The graph&apos;s purpose is informational rather than aesthetic. It&apos;s structured by quarters to illustrate fluctuations in profit and cost within each year. A negative change in profit indicates a loss for that quarter, while a positive change represents a gain. Similarly, a negative cost signifies a reduction in production expenses compared to the previous quarter, whereas a positive cost indicates an increase.

Analysis: It appears that costs have remained relatively stable over the past three years, with expected fluctuations during certain seasons, likely influenced by holidays and promotional discounts. However, profit experienced a significant decline in Q1 of 2019, possibly attributable to the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic. As the pandemic led to widespread layoffs and financial uncertainty, consumer spending decreased, resulting in a substantial drop in profit in Q2 of 2020.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Categories Sheet+ (Regional_Sales) (2)' name='federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6'>
            <column caption='Number of Orders' datatype='integer' name='[Calculation_1199083456277729280]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='COUNT([OrderNumber])' />
            </column>
            <column caption='Unit Profit' datatype='real' name='[Calculation_1199083456279875585]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='SUM(([UnitPrice]-[UnitCost])*[OrderQuantity])' />
            </column>
            <column caption='Total Cost ' datatype='real' name='[Calculation_975029375894609921]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='SUM([UnitCost]*[OrderQuantity])' />
            </column>
            <column caption='Cost Indicator' datatype='string' name='[Calculation_975029376642990087]' role='measure' type='nominal'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='IF (([Calculation_975029375894609921]) - LOOKUP(ZN([Calculation_975029375894609921]), -1))&lt;0 OR &#13;&#10;ZN([Calculation_1199083456279875585]) - LOOKUP(ZN([Calculation_1199083456279875585]), -1) &lt;0&#13;&#10;THEN &quot;Red&quot; &#13;&#10;ELSE &quot;Green&quot; &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;END'>
                <table-calc ordering-type='Rows' />
              </calculation>
            </column>
            <column datatype='string' name='[Category]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column caption='Order Date' datatype='date' name='[OrderDate]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
            <column caption='Order Number' datatype='string' name='[OrderNumber]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column caption='Order Quantity' datatype='integer' name='[OrderQuantity]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[State]' role='dimension' semantic-role='[State].[Name]' type='nominal' />
