    <worksheet name='Dual Axis Num Orders/Profit by Date'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966'>Number of Orders/Profit by Date: Jonathan Williams</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Chart Type: Line Graph
Dual Axis: Y
Reference Line: N
Trend Line: N
Calculated Fields: 2 (Number of Orders, Unit Profit)
Table Calculations: 0
LOD Calculations: 0
Mark Cards: 1
Filters: 0
Visualization: The choice of this graph prioritized functionality over aesthetics, aiming to illustrate the changes in unit profit alongside sales over the years.

Analysis: The visualization reveals that the number of orders over time seems to be stabilizing around 250 orders, indicating reduced oscillation. However, unit profit shows minimal variation across the years. From this, we can infer that while our clients are purchasing fewer items, we have likely adjusted our prices upward to offset the decrease in sales volume.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
