    <worksheet name='Median Income Pie Chart'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#8cd17d' fontsize='12'>Top Five Average Median Income by State</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#59a14f'>: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='12'>Jonathan Williams</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Chart Type: Pie Chart
Dual Axis: N
Reference Line: N
Trend Line: N
Calculated Fields: 0
Table Calculations: 0
LOD Calculations: 0
Mark Cards: 4
Filters: 1
Visualization: I opted for green and gold colors, as they are commonly associated with wealth. The lighter shade represents higher income levels. Each segment of the pie chart is labeled with the median income to avoid confusion. Initially, I included a color palette for each state, but for simplicity, I decided to display only the state names alongside the median income.

Analysis: Based on the data, the top five states exhibited a median income exceeding $55,000. This suggests that these states might be prime targets for increased advertising investments, considering their higher spending capacity compared to others.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
