  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name='Product Analysis Story' type='storyboard'>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='592' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='964' maxwidth='1016' minheight='964' minwidth='1016' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98340' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='830'>
            <zone h='4357' id='3' type-v2='title' w='98426' x='787' y='830' />
            <zone fixed-size='187' h='19398' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98426' x='787' y='5187' />
            <zone h='74585' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='24585'>
              <flipboard active-id='3' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='To address my inquiries concerning this data, I began by examining the sales and profits nationwide, categorized by state. Additionally, I reviewed the top five highest-earning states&apos; incomes and analyzed a histogram illustrating median income, which can be filtered by year and region. From this analysis, it&apos;s evident that the majority of our sales originate from the East and West Coasts, with the highest-income states correlating to the most significant sales and profits.' captured-sheet='Product Analysis Summary' id='1'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Sales and Profit by State Map'>
                        <style delta-type='added'>
                          <style-rule element='axis'>
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[Latitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='7211080.1606189618' min='2188237.6777138687' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='rows' type='space' />
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[Longitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='-2149860.307703089' min='-24693558.512799997' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='cols' type='space' />
                          </style-rule>
                        </style>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Subsequently, I delved into identifying which products incur the highest costs. By examining a barchart, we can discern the most expensive products within specific categories, which can further be segmented by year. It&apos;s notable that technology products seem to rank among the most costly items to manufacture, as indicated by the data.' captured-sheet='Cost of Production by Category' id='2'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Cost of Production by Category'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[yr:OrderDate:ok]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:OrderDate:ok]' member='2020' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Continuing from our previous analysis, we can now identify which products yield a substantial profit despite their production costs. Fortunately, we observe that there aren&apos;t many product categories underperforming. However, it would be advantageous to diversify our product range with items that are more cost-effective to manufacture.' captured-sheet='Unit Cost/Profit Quadrant Chart' id='3'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Unit Cost/Profit Quadrant Chart'>
                        <annotations>
                          <annotation delta-type='removed' id='9' />
                        </annotations>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Over time, it seems that sales have remained relatively consistent over the past two years, with a stable trend.' captured-sheet='Profit/Cost/Sales Line Chart' id='8'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Profit/Cost/Sales Line Chart'>
                        <style delta-type='added'>
                          <style-rule element='axis'>
                            <format attr='title' class='0' field='[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[usr:Calculation_975029376587993090:qk]' scope='rows' value='Sales' />
                          </style-rule>
                        </style>
                        <selection-collection>
                          <node-selection select-tuples='false'>
                            <oriented-node-reference orientation='vertical'>
                              <node-reference>
                                <axis>[federated.04m21m90b9c0ae14dtpqc1asy8f6].[usr:Calculation_975029376587993090:qk]</axis>
                              </node-reference>
                              <page-reference />
                            </oriented-node-reference>
                          </node-selection>
                        </selection-collection>
                      </worksheet>
                      <datasource name='Parameters'>
                        <column alias='Sales' name='[Parameter 1]' value='&quot;Sales&quot;' />
                      </datasource>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Nevertheless, profit is exhibiting a downward trend, prompting the need for a thorough investigation into strategies to either boost sales or streamline manufacturing costs promptly. While our overall sales performance remains strong, it&apos;s imperative to consider future growth strategies that focus on expanding sales nationwide, reducing our reliance on a select few states along the East and West Coasts.' captured-sheet='Profit/Cost/Sales Line Chart' id='9' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
